WEBVTT

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.330
Pamyunmyunmyun.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.330
"Celebrating Shirobaco's

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.330
Third Opening Anniversary"

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.000
What to do?

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.370
You're still not sure what to do for the third anniversary event?

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:12.840
It's only two days away now.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.380
We have a freshly written reading theater script to perform, don't we?

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.250
What more do we need?

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.420
I get it! I get it, Manager!

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.350
Doing reading theater would just be business as usual!

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.520
Exactly! We only get one third anniversary, after all!

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.030
I want something more special and surprising for it!

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:34.200
Yeah. So, how about we make a movie, then?

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.370
Hey! If we're making a movie,
I want a splatter film!

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.440
Tsutomu can get mauled by zombies!

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:42.440
And he can explode, too!

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:42.470
"Caution: Gore"

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.710
Do I have no human rights?!

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.910
I might enjoy a splatter movie.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:50.550
Huh? Bring on the zombies!

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.710
A movie...

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:55.580
You don't need to say what type of movie you want. We know al--

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.890
"Legend of the Asagaya Savior"

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.090
That was fast!

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.590
Well, I...

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:04.730
I'd like to be the sword the savior pulls from a stone!

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.560
You're shooting way too low!
Demand a personality, at least!

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:08.900
Whoa!

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:12.970
Y-You're putting in too much!
The eye! The eye!

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:17.410
He will vanish. And it will be your fault.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.480
Just what was that?

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.970
That voice, too... I'm sure I've heard it before.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:33.660
What's wrong?

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.260
I●●●

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:38.090
I will save Akira.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:46.540
<i>The world is engulfed by an unvoiced scream</i>

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:52.480
<i>and I wait for it to reach and stir</i> <i>a certain someone's heart</i>

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:58.280
<i>With strength flowing to the edges of our souls</i>

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:04.550
<i>we set out into the white</i> <i>morning haze, without hesitation</i>

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:07.490
<i>I want to know everything about you</i>

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:17.490
<i>But just when I thought</i>
<i>I had you, you were gone</i>

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:26.580
<i>It's love, affection, passion, expression</i>

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:33.180
<i>These tightly-sealed, silent lips</i>

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:37.550
<i>gently reply back in kind</i>

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:41.820
<i>And with love, affection, passion, expression</i>

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:48.330
<i>Now, from the last of the words I couldn't find,</i>

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:57.030
<i>the music begins</i>

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:11.690
"Know It! The Reason You Were Born"

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.020
"Enter your Password!

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.020
We don't guarantee you'll survive if

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.020
you get it wrong three times, though!"

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:16.060
Deava is a special agency made to resist Nesta and the M.J.B.K.s.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:21.560
If Akira's problem is due to writing, we must have data on it.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.200
That's risky, you know.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.260
Access things you aren't allowed to, and you'll trigger the security system.

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:35.040
What were you doing? I'm sure you weren't playing around, at least.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.780
Commander, I'd like to ask for your help!

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.270
Out of my respect for you as a man!

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.920
I'm a woman.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.560
From the outside, it looks like an ordinary library.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:51.730
But beneath it...

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.760
There is a government facility

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:59.130
collecting materials on the ancient writing culture.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.800
There's so much here.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:06.410
Even this is only a small fragment of the material that's been excavated.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:10.410
Because the vast majority has fallen into Nesta's hands.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.750
Finish your business quickly.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.820
If we get caught, I'm the one who'll be in trouble.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:17.490
Don't you worry.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:20.420
If you get canned, I'll hire you at Shirobaco.

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:22.930
Hasn't Kento always been Shirobaco staff?

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:25.960
I'm on loan from the government.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.360
I'm in charge of managing this site, as well.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:34.100
If there's something going wrong with Akira's body,

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:37.670
it's highly likely it has to do with Vector-Ga.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.810
I thought it might be that Vector...

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:41.840
It's our fault, then.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.950
We knew that machine was dangerous.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.280
True enough.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:50.120
But he piloted it of his own free will in order to save the world.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.620
"Seek"

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:53.320
So, regretting that he did isn't what we need to be doing now.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:55.520
Let's do the best we can.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:58.790
We won't let him be sacrificed. Not ever!

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.630
Oh, that's an abstract image depicting the Writing War.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:07.470
Writing War?

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:14.010
They say there was a time when people could make manifest words they spoke.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:17.980
For instance, by speaking the word "rain,"

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:20.980
they could actually make it rain.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:23.820
No way. That was really possible?

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:26.190
In the right place at the right time,

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:31.720
by speaking words filled with emotion, they accessed the world of truth.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:38.000
However, for those people who lived moment to moment,

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.000
they had no means to leave anything to future generations.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.910
They wanted to convey and leave behind their wills.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:48.040
That desire led them to create a certain something.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:49.850
And that was...

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:51.710
That was writing.

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:53.550
With writing enabling communication

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:56.750
with those far away or in later generations,

00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:00.520
civilization evolved at an accelerated pace.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.860
However, there was one tribe that felt this was dangerous.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:07.530
They worried that reliance on writing

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:12.200
would lead us to lose our connection to the world of truth.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:15.040
There were those who wished to develop the culture of writing

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:18.210
and those who were firm in their worship of the world of truth.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:21.040
Eventually, they began to fight.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:24.410
The Writing War is what is said to have happened when they did.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.580
I never knew.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:29.920
Master Sougon never told me anything...

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:32.550
He must have felt the knowledge wasn't necessary for you.

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:35.720
To create blind followers, you limit the knowledge you give them

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:38.160
to narrow their viewpoint.

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:40.930
About that woman.

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:43.600
It seems she was symbolic of something.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.630
But we don't know the exact details.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:48.900
However, the giants following her

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:52.640
are referred to in the records as "destroying angels," it seems.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:57.310
The war ultimately ended in the victory of the Writing Tribe.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:01.250
Many things remain unclear in what led to that point.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:03.920
However, there is one thing we do know.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:06.820
The thing which ended that battle.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.750
Its name was...

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.590
...Aquarion Logos.

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:18.600
Aquarion Logos.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:22.270
What is this feeling?

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:27.140
Aquarion Logos... I know that name...

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:31.280
In the end, we couldn't find anything.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:33.780
Commander, about Akira...

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:37.790
I know. I won't tell the other members of the Verbalism Club.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.960
Including Akira himself.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.960
Not even Akira?

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:46.660
We could warn him about Vector-Ga and forbid him from launching...

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:48.530
--It would be pointless.
--Hm?

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:51.370
He'll fight, no matter what you tell him.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.360
That's just how he is.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:56.370
"Limited Time Only Menu

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:56.370
Item Idea Proposal Meeting"

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:58.210
We'll be targeting our female customers.

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:01.480
Women love things that are "for a limited time only," after all!

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:04.350
Y-Yeah, that will get them lining up.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:07.320
The limited-time menu should have many healthy items,

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.150
since those are popular with women.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:11.390
When you say "healthy," do you mean like salads?

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:15.560
You can't fill up on that stuff!
Let's offer something more hardy!

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:16.990
Like fried chicken!

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:18.160
Rejected.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:22.530
Not only are fried foods the opposite of healthy, they take time to prepare.

00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:24.030
--The chickens...
--Huh?

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:25.030
How about I raise them?

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.170
Why would we start by raising livestock ourselves?

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:30.840
Big Brother Hayato!
I want to have hamburger steaks!

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.240
What a little kid...

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.510
--Huh? Shut up!
--Yowch!

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:36.580
I see. Hamburger steaks, huh?

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:37.750
Cows, huh?

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.680
Y-You don't have to raise them, okay?

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:43.920
Then how about we make healthy hamburger steaks?

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.550
I agree!

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:48.020
Sakurako loves her hamburger steaks!

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:52.730
Okay! Let's all create our own original healthy hamburger steaks now!

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:55.030
What?! We're making them?!

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:57.090
Everyone will participate.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:02.600
The boys' hamburger steaks are ready!

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:05.410
Hayato's is a tofu burger, huh?

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:06.880
That's a classic.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:10.080
Th-The shape of Tsutomu's...

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:13.150
Is this even a hamburger steak?

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.880
I'm glad you asked!

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.120
Making a hamburger steak out of tofu is kind of plain, you know?

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:21.060
So I made a tofu out of hamburger!

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.960
That's just a square-ish lump of meat!

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:26.060
Akira's looks pretty plain.

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:29.900
Well, it looks fine, but the taste is what counts!

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.400
Huh? What's this?

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.930
The texture is kind of...

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:39.160
"Low Calorie"

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:40.580
I tried putting this in.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.780
Make something <i>edible</i>, at least.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:46.320
It looks like Hayato's the only one who'll be any use.

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:49.420
Now it's the girls' turn! Come on!

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:52.090
Kokone and Maia, let's hurry!

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:53.990
Cooking is beyond me...

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:57.160
If you make one for him,
I'll bet Akira will be happy.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:59.130
Huh?

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:01.430
--Come on, try eating it yourself!
--Don't rush me.

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:03.130
I'll eat it. For I am...

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:08.440
Maia, you're kneading too hard.

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:10.670
This is tough...

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:13.140
More like this. See?

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:15.280
Like this?

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:18.510
Yeah! Like you're throttling a M.J.B.K. to death!

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:19.510
I get it now!

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:22.220
Karan! Don't lie to her!

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:24.450
I'll finish you, M.J.B.K.!

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:27.460
Strike!

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.550
Don't take her seriously!

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:37.370
Whoa! Awesome!

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:39.300
Where did you learn to do that?

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:54.520
Wow! That looks tasty!

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:57.650
What?! Why'd you throw it away?

00:10:57.650 --> 00:11:02.160
I... I messed up on the spices...

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:05.920
N-No one could eat it, so...

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.760
I did it! It's ready!

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.680
What do you think?

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:21.080
Akira?

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:24.180
I will find a way... to save my stomach!

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:25.350
What a cliché!

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:28.020
You could just say it tasted bad!

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:30.890
Maia sure has changed.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:35.090
She's just turned back into a regular girl her age.

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:58.610
You used too many ingredients.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:00.050
Oh, hush!

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:03.450
I'm making up for it by going to pick up more myself.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.750
You're so high-maintenance.

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:08.060
You tagged along on your own!

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:10.230
Should I not have?

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:13.400
I don't mind... that you did...

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:15.800
--Want to sit down for a bit?
--Huh?

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:17.900
Aren't they taking a little long for just shopping?

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:21.070
They'd better not be off whispering sweet nothings to one another!

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:25.110
You're jealous? Even when you have such a cute girlfriend?

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:26.480
What's this?

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:29.310
I made this separately from the ones for taste-testing.

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:31.480
It's a lunch for you.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:33.120
Shoko!

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:33.750
Dodged!

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:35.580
Why?

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:38.420
Oh! Are you okay?

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:40.090
I... I'm sorry.

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:42.260
Did something happen?

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:45.590
I... I'm just feeling a little ill.

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:51.330
What's with this situation?

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.830
I wanted to ask you something.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:53.940
Huh?!

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:55.770
About Subete Kenzaki.

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:59.980
Are you curious what kind of relationship he and I had?

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:02.440
I can't let him be better than me.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:04.980
Next time we meet, he's going down.

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:07.820
To that end, I want to know. About him.

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:10.290
Oh, that's all.

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:12.120
--What?
--Nothing.

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:13.820
Huh?

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:17.160
Subete's psyche is somewhat uneven.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:21.700
He's highly capable, but his immaturity holds him back.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:23.470
He's not able to bring his full power to bear.

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:26.970
Despite that, he's overconfident.
He has a lot of openings.

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:30.040
He lets his guard down too easily.
He lacks the ability to make decisions.

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:32.300
There wasn't a single good trait there.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:38.350
But it's not like he's a bad guy.
He had things going for him, too.

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:40.050
After all, a long time ago...

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:41.050
A long time ago?

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:46.220
Back then, on a beautiful moonlit night like this...

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:51.360
...I was hopelessly sad, suffering so much,
I wished I could disappear.

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:53.230
I was crying.

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:54.820
That was when...

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:01.240
I don't remember what Subete said to me.

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:04.670
But his words saved me.

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:07.340
They let me feel it was okay to go on living.

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:08.680
Hm...

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:09.850
What is it?

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:11.080
Nothing.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:13.050
What? What are you mad about?

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:15.580
Nothing. Let's get going already.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:17.680
Uh... Hey!

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:39.270
What's wrong?

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.040
No, nothing...

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:43.530
Yeah?

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:53.480
I don't want to lose him. Not Akira...

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:59.260
I won't let you vanish!

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:00.990
Not ever!

00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:16.950
At Nesta, they should have far more resources on the writing culture.

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:20.750
There must be one! A way to save Akira!

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:25.090
Odd.

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:28.920
They must have noticed by now, but security's doing nothing.

00:15:32.590 --> 00:15:35.600
Took you long enough.

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:37.270
Subete.

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:40.600
You must have anticipated I would be here.

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:43.840
Despite that, you rated me as no impediment to your search.

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:48.780
You planned to hold me down and use me as a hostage to make your escape.

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:50.980
You underestimated me.

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:51.980
Why?!

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:53.480
How does he know, you mean?

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:56.620
That ought to be obvious!

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:59.050
Because you are me.

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:01.320
You're...!

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:05.130
Oh, lovely! You can see me properly!

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.120
Though that ought to be a given.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:10.960
This is the first time we've properly met.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:15.070
"Celebrating Our Third Opening Anniversary"

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:15.970
Here's to three years!

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:18.810
It's not time yet! No jumping the gun!

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:21.010
I'm ready to go as long as Kokone's here!

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:23.850
Hayato! I'll take mine with a double serving of hunkiness!

00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:25.640
Not until everyone's here.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:30.520
Why are Maia and Akira not here?

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:33.490
Maia wasn't at Digibaco, either.

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:35.890
Where could she have gone, meow?

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:37.830
Akira...

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:53.240
You again?

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:58.710
You came here alone to save
Akira Kaibuki. How devoted.

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:01.380
Do you know something?

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:06.690
What is trying to erase Akira Kaibuki is the power you people call Vector-Ga.

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:11.760
That accursed power devours concepts and erases them.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:16.360
At this rate, the concept known as Akira Kaibuki will vanish.

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:18.960
Do you understand what that means?

00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:23.710
With his concept lost, no one will be able to see him.

00:17:23.710 --> 00:17:27.380
He will become imperceptible.
And that's not all.

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:31.080
Eventually, his existence will vanish from memory.

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:32.750
The time you spent together,

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:36.890
the memories you share, will slip from your mind.

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:41.090
Eventually, Akira Kaibuki will disappear from inside you, as well.

00:17:41.090 --> 00:17:44.390
That can't be... Akira will...

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:45.890
You sad?

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:50.270
Well, you have no right to feel that way!

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:51.730
Didn't I tell you?

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:54.800
His disappearance is your fault!

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:58.470
Akira Kaibuki is taking your place.

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:01.480
--I will devour.
--Don't... Come out...

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:02.740
Devour.

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:04.610
Stay inside me.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:13.460
After all, the one Vector-Ga truly wants to erase...

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:15.320
...is you.

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:21.660
Vector-Ga was created to defeat Aquarion Logos.

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:27.500
And that raison d'être still lives on, even 12,000 years later.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.270
What do you...

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:33.780
When Aquarion Logos appeared in the middle of the Writing War,

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:36.470
there were two people aboard it.

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:41.620
One of those two was myself, Nesta.

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:42.680
Nesta?

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:47.020
And the other pilot was the one I loved.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:50.020
Kiryu.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:52.790
Aquarion Logos fell in battle,

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:55.160
and Kiryu and I both died.

00:18:55.160 --> 00:19:00.030
However, in the present, a person who desired our power appeared.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.300
My father.

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:03.840
Master Sougon?

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:08.710
Dad needed Aquarion Logos's power.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:12.210
And so, after 12,000 years,

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:16.510
he acquired the person born under the right stars to become Kiryu.

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:19.820
You can't mean...

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:23.490
Yes, him. Subete Kenzaki is the one.

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:28.200
He has inherited the legacy of
Aquarion Logos's former pilot, Kiryu.

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:29.830
And...

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:31.830
To be with Subete.

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:35.670
That is the reason you were born.

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:39.670
Using my soul which had dissolved into the Logos World,

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:43.040
he created another being that would act as the key.

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:44.910
With Subete's power.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:46.050
I don't want to hear this!

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:47.680
This is...

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:50.020
It's coming! We've succeeded!

00:19:55.590 --> 00:20:00.260
With Verbalism as the catalyst, you were formed from Nesta's soul.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.700
A puppet made with Verbalism, you could say.

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:06.230
That is what you are, Maia.

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:08.640
I-It can't be true...

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:16.040
You're not even human.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:18.110
You're just a replacement for me.

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:20.210
My pretty puppet.

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:23.380
...you're nothing more than a puppet.

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:26.550
That's a lie!

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:35.300
I didn't know until I took the
Book of Verbalism's power into myself.

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:38.600
No, it would be more correct to say I'd forgotten.

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:41.570
My memories of your origin were all sealed.

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:43.070
Subete...

00:20:43.070 --> 00:20:46.070
But now I remember everything.

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:50.250
Including how I created you from the Logos World as my father watched.

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:53.650
The moment of your birth, your parents...

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:55.920
Have you ever tried to remember them?

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.990
I'll bet not!

00:20:57.990 --> 00:21:02.090
You were created not to think of such things, after all!

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:04.580
Shut up! Stop!

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:15.100
Did she make the sky cry?

00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:18.340
This is the power of truth.

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:23.340
By being with Subete, you manifested a power you never could have alone.

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:28.620
Limited though it may be, that is the same power as mine.

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:33.180
But you must understand now. What you are.

00:21:41.130 --> 00:21:43.030
O wretched puppet,

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:47.140
I will at least end it without you suffering.

00:21:47.140 --> 00:21:50.140
It's pouring outside.

00:21:50.140 --> 00:21:53.730
No fair! It's our anniversary!

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:57.310
Huh? Oh.

00:21:57.310 --> 00:22:00.380
Akira? Y-You were here?

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:02.380
Where's Maia?

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:04.320
--What?!
--Huh?!

00:22:09.990 --> 00:22:15.200
Yes, let us end it. This battle.

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:17.170
This world.

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:25.770
<i>I want to lend you a true voice</i>

00:22:35.850 --> 00:22:41.190
<i>With the warmth of salvation,</i>
<i>I raise my hand into the sky</i>

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:45.930
<i>and everything in the world gains its true colors</i>

00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:48.600
<i>(Focus) A sound that was once hidden</i>

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:51.700
<i>(on the goal) will connect us now</i>

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:54.200
<i>Try to understand that, okay?</i>

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:56.640
<i>So, are you ready?</i>

00:22:56.640 --> 00:22:59.440
<i>(heart and soul) These silent teardrops</i>

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:02.040
<i>(narrow escape) that flow forth now</i>

00:23:02.040 --> 00:23:05.550
<i>(enamored) are proof of that person's existence</i>

00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:12.050
<i>You can't go inside your heart all alone</i>

00:23:12.050 --> 00:23:14.620
<i>I will hesitate no more</i>

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:19.790
<i>I want to lend you a true voice</i>

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:25.000
<i>A useful life, a sparkling utopia</i>

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:34.110
<i>When your heart and voice</i> <i>tremble together, you'll surpass all</i>

00:23:34.110 --> 00:23:37.510
<i>So go for your heart</i>

00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:51.790
Shoko, look at this!

00:23:51.790 --> 00:23:53.930
It's Okinawa's famous top-quality <i>chinsuko</i> biscuits!

00:23:53.930 --> 00:23:56.160
--Wow!
--Tsutomu, you're way too excited.

00:23:56.160 --> 00:23:58.330
I just want to see my girlfriend's smile.

00:23:58.330 --> 00:23:59.770
Mind your own business, squirt!

00:23:59.770 --> 00:24:00.940
Who're you calling a squirt?!

00:24:00.940 --> 00:24:03.440
Oh, Tsutomu, there are crumbs around your mouth.

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:04.440
Oh!

00:24:04.440 --> 00:24:06.340
Next time, Episode 21!

00:24:04.870 --> 00:24:08.110
"Episode 21: Tragic! An Immoral Gattai"

00:24:06.340 --> 00:24:08.310
"Tragic! An Immoral Gattai."

00:24:08.310 --> 00:24:09.800
Ugh, lovebirds.
